<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>URL Shortener Documentation</title>
    <style>
@page {
    size: A4;
    margin: 2cm;
}

body {
    width: 21cm;
    min-height: 29.7cm;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2.5cm;
    background: white;
    color: #333;
    font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;
    line-height: 1.4;
    font-size: 12pt;
}

h1 {
    font-size: 24pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-align: center;
    margin: 0 0 36pt;
    border-bottom: 2pt solid #000;
    padding-bottom: 12pt;
}

h2 {
    font-size: 14pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    margin: 24pt 0 12pt;
    page-break-after: avoid;
}

h3 {
    font-size: 12pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    margin: 12pt 0 6pt;
    color: #444;
    margin-top: 18pt;
}

.doc-section {
    margin: 18pt 0;
    padding: 12pt;
    border: 0.5pt solid #ddd;
    page-break-inside: avoid;
}

.feature-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 12pt 0;
}

.feature-table th,
.feature-table td {
    border: 0.5pt solid #ddd;
    padding: 6pt;
    vertical-align: top;
}

.feature-table th {
    background: #f8f8f8;
    font-weight: bold;
}

.tech-stack {
    margin: 12pt 0;
}

.tech-card {
    margin: 6pt 0;
    padding: 6pt;
    border-left: 3pt solid #000;
}

.process-steps {
    margin: 12pt 0 0;
}

.step {
    margin: 0 0 12pt 12pt;
    padding-left: 12pt;
    border-left: 1pt solid #000;
}

footer {
    position: fixed;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 12pt 0;
    border-top: 1pt solid #ddd;
}

.footer-content {
    max-width: 21cm;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 2.5cm;
    font-size: 10pt;
    color: #666;
}

@media print {
    body {
        padding: 2cm;
    }
    
    .doc-section {
        border: none;
        padding: 0;
    }
    
    footer {
        position: fixed;
    }
}

.spec-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 12pt 0;
}

.spec-table td, .spec-table th {
    border: 1pt solid #000;
    padding: 6pt;
}

pre {
    background: #f8f8f8;
    border: 0.5pt solid #ddd;
    padding: 12pt;
    margin: 12pt 0;
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 10pt;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
}

ul {
    margin: 12pt 0;
    padding-left: 24pt;
}

li {
    margin: 6pt 0;
}

.tech-stack-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 18pt 0;
}

.tech-stack-table td, .tech-stack-table th {
    border: 1pt solid #000;
    padding: 8pt;
    text-align: left;
}

ol {
    margin: 12pt 0;
    padding-left: 24pt;
}
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>URL Shortener Service Documentation<br><small>Technical Deep Dive</small></h1>

    <div class="doc-section">
        <h2>1. Feature Breakdown</h2>
        <h3>Core Features</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>URL Shortening:</strong> Convert long URLs to 6-8 character codes using Base62 encoding</li>
            <li><strong>Custom Aliases:</strong> Users can create memorable short codes (3-20 chars)</li>
            <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> Track total clicks, referrers, and timestamps</li>
            <li><strong>QR Codes:</strong> Generate printable QR codes for each short URL</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h3>Advanced Features</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Link Expiration:</strong> Set TTL from 1 hour to 1 year</li>
            <li><strong>Bulk Import:</strong> CSV upload for mass URL shortening</li>
            <li><strong>API Access:</strong> REST endpoints for integration</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-section">
        <h2>2. Technology Stack</h2>
        <table class="tech-stack-table">
            <tr>
                <th>Layer</th>
                <th>Technology</th>
                <th>Purpose</th>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Frontend</td>
                <td>EJS + Bootstrap</td>
                <td>Server-side rendered UI</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Backend</td>
                <td>Node.js + Express</td>
                <td>Routing and business logic</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Database</td>
                <td>MongoDB</td>
                <td>Store URLs and analytics</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Caching</td>
                <td>Redis</td>
                <td>Rate limiting and hot data</td>
            </tr>
        </table>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-section">
        <h2>3. Use Case Analysis</h2>
        <h3>Primary Use Cases</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Social Media Marketing:</strong> Shorten links for Twitter/X</li>
            <li><strong>Email Campaigns:</strong> Track click-through rates</li>
            <li><strong>Printed Materials:</strong> QR codes for posters/flyers</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h3>Enterprise Usage</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Internal link management for large organizations</li>
            <li>API integration with marketing automation tools</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-section">
        <h2>4. Development Challenges</h2>
        <h3>Technical Hurdles</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Collision Handling:</strong> Ensuring unique short codes</li>
            <li><strong>Scale:</strong> Supporting 10k+ req/sec</li>
            <li><strong>Validation:</strong> Sanitizing user inputs</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h3>Solutions Implemented</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Base62 encoding with collision fallback</li>
            <li>Redis-based rate limiting</li>
            <li>Regular expression validation</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-section">
        <h2>5. Implementation Strategy</h2>
        <h3>Development Phases</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Core Shortening (Week 1-2)</li>
            <li>Analytics System (Week 3)</li>
            <li>QR Generation (Week 4)</li>
            <li>API Endpoints (Week 5)</li>
        </ol>
        
        <h3>Testing Approach</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Jest for unit tests</li>
            <li>Load testing with Artillery</li>
            <li>Security audit with OWASP ZAP</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <footer>
        <div class="footer-content">
            Implementation Date: <%= new Date().toLocaleDateString() %><br>
            Author: Prince | Document Version: 1.0
        </div>
    </footer>
</body>
</html> 